---
/**
 * Privacy Policy – englische Fassung der Datenschutzerklärung (Runde 8).
 * Nur zur Information; rechtlich maßgeblich ist die deutsche Fassung (Hinweis auf der Seite).
 * Gleiche Inhalte und offene Platzhalter wie src/views/Datenschutz.astro – bei Änderungen beide anpassen.
 *
 * HINWEIS – KEINE GEWÄHR, KEINE RECHTSBERATUNG: vor Veröffentlichung fachkundig prüfen lassen.
 */
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Hero from "../components/sections/Hero.astro";
import Rechtstext from "../components/sections/Rechtstext.astro";
import { firma } from "../lib/config";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy of Selim-IT: what data is processed when you visit this website, send an enquiry or book an appointment, and what rights you have."
  pfad="/datenschutz"
>
  <Hero
    kompakt
    headline="Privacy Policy"
    subline="What data we process when you use this website or get in touch with us, and what rights you have."
  />

  <Rechtstext stand="September 16, 2026">
    <p class="rt__hinweis">
      This English version is provided for convenience only. The <a href="/datenschutz" hreflang="de" lang="de">German version</a>
      is legally binding.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Controller</h2>
    <p>The controller responsible for data processing on this website is:</p>
    <address class="rt__karte">
      {firma.name}, owner {firma.inhaber}<br />
      {firma.adresse.strasse},{" "}
      <span class:list={{ platzhalter: firma.adresse.plz.platzhalter }}>{firma.adresse.plz.platzhalter ? "[postal code to follow]" : firma.adresse.plz.wert}</span>
      {" "}{firma.adresse.stadt}, Germany<br />
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${firma.email.adresse}`}>{firma.email.adresse}</a><br />
      Phone:{" "}
      {firma.telefon.platzhalter ? <span class="platzhalter">[phone number to follow]</span> : <a href={firma.telefon.href}>{firma.telefon.anzeige}</a>}
    </address>

    <h2>2. Hosting and server log files</h2>
    <p>
      This website runs on our own infrastructure in Germany. When you visit the website, the server automatically stores
      information transmitted by your browser: IP address, date and time of the request, the page requested, the referrer URL,
      and your browser type and operating system.
    </p>
    <p>
      We use this data to operate the website securely and reliably and to defend against attacks. The legal basis is our
      legitimate interest under Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. The log files are deleted automatically after{" "}
      <span class="platzhalter">[retention period to be defined]</span>. All data is transmitted in encrypted form only
      (HTTPS/TLS).
    </p>

    <h2>3. Fonts</h2>
    <p>All fonts are served directly from our own server. No connection is made to third-party servers (such as Google Fonts).</p>

    <h2>4. Cookie-free audience measurement</h2>
    <p>
      We use self-hosted, cookie-free analytics software (<span class="platzhalter">[Umami or Plausible, to be decided]</span>).
      No cookies are set, no individual usage profiles are created and IP addresses are not stored. The legal basis is our
      legitimate interest in statistical analysis to improve our services (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). No consent is required for this,
      as no cookies are set and no information is stored on your device.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Enquiry form</h2>
    <p>
      If you contact us via the enquiry form, we process the information you provide: the topics and details you select,
      urgency, company size, your message, your first and last name, optionally your company and phone number, and your email
      address. This information is stored in a dedicated database on our infrastructure in Germany and also sent to us by
      email so that we can handle your enquiry and refer back to it if we have any questions.
    </p>
    <p>
      The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR where your enquiry relates to a contract or pre-contractual measures, and otherwise
      our legitimate interest in responding to enquiries (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). We do not pass this data on without your consent.
      It is deleted as soon as it is no longer needed to handle your enquiry, and at the latest after{" "}
      <span class="platzhalter">[storage period to be defined]</span>, unless statutory retention obligations apply.
    </p>
    <p>
      To protect against automated spam, we use an invisible check field and Altcha, a self-hosted spam protection that works
      without cookies or external services. Your browser solves a small computational task; no personal data is transferred to
      third parties for this purpose. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in preventing misuse (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
    </p>

    <h2>6. Appointment booking (free initial consultation)</h2>
    <p>
      If you book an initial consultation via the form, we process your details and the selected time slot to coordinate the
      appointment in a self-hosted Nextcloud calendar (CalDAV). For the video call, a room is created automatically in our
      self-hosted Nextcloud Talk. We do not use external providers such as Google Calendar, Zoom or Microsoft Teams, and no data
      is transferred to third countries. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Email communication</h2>
    <p>
      We send confirmation and reply emails through our own mail server, without an external mailing service. If you write to
      us by email, we process your details in order to deal with your request (Art. 6(1)(b) or (f) GDPR).
    </p>

    <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
    <p>You have the right at any time to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>access the data we hold about you (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
      <li>have inaccurate data corrected (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
      <li>have your data erased (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
      <li>restrict processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
      <li>data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
      <li>object to processing based on legitimate interests (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To exercise these rights, simply contact us using the details above.</p>

    <h2>9. Right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority</h2>
    <p>You have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority. The authority responsible for us is:</p>
    <address class="rt__karte">
      The Hessian Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information (HBDI)<br />
      P.O. Box 3163, 65021 Wiesbaden, Germany
    </address>
  </Rechtstext>
</BaseLayout>
